  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ノゲシ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8E%E3%82%B2%E3%82%B7",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 109588172,
      "text": "ノゲシ とは、キク科ノゲシ属の植物の一種。別名ハルノノゲシ、ケシアザミ、チチグサ、ウマアザミ。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Sonchus oleraceus",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1373258847,
      "text": "Sonchus oleraceus is a species of flowering plant in the tribe Cichorieae of the family Asteraceae, native to Europe and Western Asia. It has many common names including common sowthistle, sow thistle, smooth sow thistle, annual sow thistle, puha, hare's colwort, hare's thistle, milky tassel, milk thistle, and soft thistle."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Sonchus oleraceus",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 172452327,
      "text": "Sonchus oleraceus, conocido comúnmente por cerraja, cerrajón o canayuyo es una especie de planta herbácea del género Sonchus en la familia Asteraceae."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Sonchus oleraceus",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 238350510,
      "text": "Sonchus oleraceus, communément appelé le Laiteron maraîcher, Laiteron commun, Laiteron lisse ou Laiteron potager, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs du genre Sonchus et de la famille des Asteraceae. L’espèce est originaire d’Europe, d’Afrique du Nord et du Moyen-Orient et a été introduite dans presque tous les autres pays du monde. C’est une plante rudérale que l’on trouve dans les champs, les jardins, les décombres, les friches, les bords de route ou les bords de trottoir en ville."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Sonchus oleraceus",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 73198388,
      "text": "A serralha, serralha-branca ou serrallha-macia é uma planta herbácea da familia Asteraceae."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Sonchus oleraceus",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 28105873,
      "text": "Sonchus oleracus adalah sebuah tanaman di suku dandelion dalam asteraceae. Tanaman ini asli ke Eropa dan Asia Barat."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "ja": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ノゲシ § 利用",
        "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8E%E3%82%B2%E3%82%B7#%E5%88%A9%E7%94%A8",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 109588172,
        "heading": "利用",
        "text": "若苗、若葉、柔らかい茎先は食用になる。一年中採取できるが、生長した葉は苦味があるため、2 - 4月ごろのまだ茎が立たないうちに、若苗は根際から株ごと、葉などは摘み取って採取される。春に採取したものは茹でてから水にとって冷ますが、時期を過ぎて苦味が出た茎葉は茹でてから水にさらしておき、おひたし、和え物、煮びたし、油炒めなどにする。若苗は生のままサラダにしたり、若葉を天ぷらする。",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Sonchus oleraceus § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1373258847,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The leaves are eaten as salad greens or cooked like spinach. This is one of the species used in Chinese cuisine as kŭcài (苦菜; lit. bitter vegetable). The younger leaves are less bitter and better to eat raw. Steaming can remove the bitterness of older leaves. The younger roots are also edible and can suffice as a coffee substitute.\n\n■ Nutrition\nNutritional analysis reveals 30–40 mg of vitamin C per 100 g of plant, 1.2% protein, 0.3% fat, 2.4% carbohydrate. Leaf dry matter analysis per 100 g (likely to vary with growing conditions) shows: 45 g carbohydrate, 28 g protein, 22 g ash, 5.9 g fibre, 4.5 g fat; in all, providing 265 calories.\nMinerals\n\nCalcium: 1500 mg\nPhosphorus: 500 mg\nIron: 45.6 mg\nMagnesium: 0 mg\nSodium: 0 mg\nPotassium: 0 mg\nZinc: 0 mg\nVitamins\n\nA: 35 mg\nThiamine (B1): 1.5 mg\nRiboflavin (B2): 5 mg\nNiacin: 5 mg\nB6: 0 mg\nC: 60 mg\n\n■ Herbalism\nSonchus oleraceus has a variety of uses in herbalism. It also has been ascribed medicinal qualities similar to dandelion and succory. When the plant was introduced to New Zealand, the Māori people found it similar to and as palatable as their native pūhā or S. kirkii (also known as raurōroa), thus also picked up S. oleraceus (since also named rauriki) for similar food and medical use.\nNative Americans had many uses for this plant. Pima used its gum as a \"cure for the opium habit\", as a cathartic, and as a food, where the \"leaves and stems [were] rubbed between the palms of the hands and eaten raw\" and sometimes \"boiled\". The Yaqui used the plant as a vegetable, where the \"tender, young leaves [were] boiled in salted water with chile and eaten as greens.\" The Kamia (Kumeyaay) \"boiled leaves for food as greens\".",
        "truncated": true
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Sonchus oleraceus § Utilisations",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus#Utilisations",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 238350510,
        "heading": "Utilisations",
        "text": "Si la racine juteuse est assez tendre, elle peut être mangée cuite. Les feuilles peuvent être consommées crues (jeunes feuilles en salades) ou cuites (feuilles plus âgées en légumes, en soupes ou étuvées à la crème). Comme les pissenlits, les boutons floraux peuvent être ajoutés crus aux salades ou conservés dans le vinaigre comme les câpres.\nÀ La Réunion, il est consommé en brède et appelé brède lastron, appellation qu'il partage avec le laiteron piquant.\nLe laiteron a des propriétés thérapeutiques comme le pissenlit (diurétique, légèrement laxative, cholérétique et cholagogue). En Tanzanie et à Madagascar, les racines sont utilisées comme purgatif et en Tanzanie comme abortif et vermifuge. \nIl est également utilisé comme fourrage. Il est apprécié par les bovins, les porcins et les lapins.\nAdventice des cultures, il est un hôte pour les maladies et les ravageurs, d'où l'usage de cette espèce comme plante piège pour assurer le suivi et la lutte contre les populations d'insectes.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "pt": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Sonchus oleraceus § Propriedades medicinais",
        "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonchus_oleraceus#Propriedades_medicinais",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 73198388,
        "heading": "Propriedades medicinais",
        "text": "Contém flavonoides\nUtilizada no tratamento de vitiligo\nUsa-se como estimulante do apetite\nAdstringente\nFortificante do sistema nervoso",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
